<speak>Yes, I confirm that is my final transaction instruction. Please proceed as you have just summarised. Thank you, Adeline. I appreciate your patience with the digressions. I know I went from the office handover to the dining table and then to the tablet charger, but those things are all connected in my head. When everyday administration becomes untidy, it makes a simple conversation feel more complicated than it should. Having time to talk through the practical side helped me slow down. I will keep this notebook for personal matters rather than putting it back into the business folder. That way I should be able to find my own reminders when I get home this evening.</speak>